        "h": "<strong>Summary:</strong> Starting a supplement brand in the US means building a regulated product business, not slapping a label on a stock formula. This guide walks through the fifteen steps in the order that saves money: define the customer, check the economics, clear the name, settle the regulatory route, qualify a manufacturer, develop the product, approve the claims and label, release the batch, then sell. It closes with a realistic timeline and a complete launch checklist."
